# Vault data lives on data/<name> branches only — never on main or feature/*.
#
# .gitignore is itself a tracked file, so each branch carries its own copy and
# git switches these rules for you on checkout. On a data/<name> branch the
# /data/ line below is removed, which is what makes the notes trackable there.
#
# .githooks/pre-push is the safety net. Enable it once per clone:
#
#     git config core.hooksPath .githooks
/data/

# A nested duplicate of the vault, left over from an earlier layout.
/MyVault/

# Only the plugins this branch develops against are tracked here. main carries
# every plugin; a feature branch carries the ones under development, so unrelated
# plugin churn never lands in these commits.
#
# Do not edit the block below by hand — run, from the repo root:
#
#     .githooks/scope-branch <plugin> [<plugin>...]
#
# Like /data/ above, this list is per-branch: main's copy of .gitignore has no
# such section. Because of that, a MERGE of this branch into main would carry
# the untracking as deletions — integrate plugin work with cherry-pick, and see
# .githooks/pre-push, which refuses a push that strips main.
# >>> scope-branch >>>
/.obsidian/plugins/*
!/.obsidian/plugins/media-viewer/
!/.obsidian/plugins/video-editor/
# <<< scope-branch <<<

# A feature branch carries the plugin and what runs it, nothing else. Vault
# content and personal appearance live on main and on data/<project> branches.
#
# Per-branch, like every rule above, with the same consequence: these paths are
# untracked here, so merging this branch into main would arrive as deletions.
# Cherry-pick, and let .githooks/pre-push catch the mistake.
/assets/
/config/
/doc/
/Operon/
/ref/
/.obsidian/snippets/
/.obsidian/themes/

# The vault settings that say who is using it rather than what the plugins need.
# Obsidian rewrites these every time it runs, so tracking them makes `git status`
# noise out of moving a pane. app.json, community-plugins.json and
# core-plugins.json stay: they are what makes a fresh clone open with both
# plugins already enabled, which is the install in README.md.
/.obsidian/appearance.json
/.obsidian/graph.json
/.obsidian/hotkeys.json
/.obsidian/workspace.json

# Written by the plugins as they run, or too large to carry. bin/ is ffmpeg —
# 290 MB and platform-specific; its README is the instruction for filling it.
# tests/ is a harness a clone re-creates, not something the vault ships.
.obsidian/plugins/media-viewer/data.json
.obsidian/plugins/media-viewer/debug.log
.obsidian/plugins/media-viewer/crash.log
.obsidian/plugins/media-viewer/tests/
.obsidian/plugins/video-editor/data.json
.obsidian/plugins/video-editor/tests/
.obsidian/plugins/video-editor/bin/*
!.obsidian/plugins/video-editor/bin/README.md
